'''Noya Media Network''' ('''NMN'''; {{Langx|kz|ߣߐߦߊ ߡߜߓߊߛߊ ߣߋߕߌߥߐߞߌ|Nọyá Mgbàsá Nẹtiwọkì}}), known simply as '''Noya''' ({{literally|knowledge}}) is a [[Sanyan|Sanyanian]] private-media [[w:Media conglomerate|conglomerate]] funded in part by the [[government of Sanyan]]. The network's flagship channels include [[Noya Imo]] and [[Noya Brieslandic]], which provide coverage of regional and international news, along with analysis, documentaries, and talk shows. In addition to its television channels, Noya has expanded its digital presence with platforms such as [[NN+]], catering to younger audiences with formats and content tailored for online consumption. Noya broadcasts in over 120 countries and territories mostly in the {{W|Global North}}, and has a large global audience of over 500 million people.

